# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The context is sent to the daemon in full before any COPY runs, so anything
# listed here never enters a build layer — which is what makes "no secret is
# present in any layer" (FR-042) a property of the build rather than a claim.
#
# This is belt-and-braces with .gitignore, deliberately. .gitignore protects
# what is committed; this protects what is shipped. They are not redundant: a
# developer's uncommitted local .env is in the build context even though it is
# not in the commit.

# --- secrets: never in any layer, committed or not -----------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# --- version control -----------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- documentation and specs: not needed to run the image ---------------------
# The image serves the API. It does not need the specification that produced it.
specs/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- local development ---------------------------------------------------------
**/.venv
venv/
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/*.egg-info

# --- data: the corpus is fetched at run time, never shipped (FR-032) ------------
data/
evaluation/
crawl-cache/
.raw/
pages/
extracted/
*.html
*.htm
*.pdf

# --- tooling -------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
node_modules/
Makefile
docker-compose*.yml
scripts/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# --- editors -------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
